         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nThe next number of the decimal system is the number two (2). The idea for building its multiplication table is exactly the same as the one we used for zero and one: multiplying by two means adding numbers 2 by 2.\n\nAnd, like every other multiplication table, this one also has a special characteristic of its own: every answer of the table of two is a doubled number — and that gives the table a special rhythm we are going to discover in this class.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
